    native_build_interpreted_worker_fixed_2_4gb_floor_2026-08-18, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep6: measured at tip - the worker now runs JIT (coordinator pins SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=jit because interpreted module loading regressed past 30 min), peak 5.61-5.67 GiB across 4 runs (the mode switch that made the worker usable tripled the floor vs the doc's 2.4 GiB); live heap only 512.7 MB of the tracked peak, ~3.1 GiB is mimalloc-parked freed pages. The prior fix commits (2878e8d2c5d, 5f0e26c00d0) are ancestors. Fix landed: the SIMPLE_MEMPROBE diagnostic from a prior lane was dead under JIT (plain-named memory_usage extern rejected by the rt_interp_call dispatch gate -> process::exit(1) at the first probe); swapped to registry-backed rt_process_rss_kib (pure-Simple, no seed rebuild, both lanes work) - full worker_entry/exit probe lines now emit. Regression gate: scripts/perf/measure-native-build-worker-floor.shs (bounded peak harness, JIT-pinned, budget 6.4M KiB, fail-closed) + test/05_perf/compiler/native_build_worker_rss_floor_spec.spl (SIMPLE_PERF_BINARY override) - spec 1/1 PASS on the scratch binary, harness peak_kib=5887676 verdict PASS. Residuals: the floor itself (transient load/JIT-compile set) needs the compiled worker / demand-driven compile pipeline (bootstrap redesign); the mem-trace census is blind on the JIT lane (instrumentation work); general seed gap: plain-named interpreter-registry-only externs are uncallable under JIT (proper fix in interp_call_uses_extern_dispatch, needs the cargo-rebuild grant). close_evidence reproducer=test/05_perf/compiler/native_build_worker_rss_floor_spec.spl prevention=scripts/perf/measure-native-build-worker-floor.shs"

